        "problem": "What is the cardinality of $K\\times L$ for $K={a,b,c,d}$ and $L={0,1,2,3,\u2026,8}?$",
        "worked_solution": "For any two finite sets $K$ and $L,$ the cardinality of $K\\times L$ is\n\n$$\n|K\\times L|=|K|\\cdot |L|.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|K\\times L| & =|K|\\cdot |L| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
